# Only hexproof is ignored. On turn five Bot1's Nowhere to Run enters trigger targets Bot2's Elvish Mystic, and Bot2 responds by
# tapping Mother of Runes for protection from black. Nowhere to Run's permission does not touch protection (CR 702.16b), so the
# target is illegal on resolution (CR 608.2b), the trigger does nothing and the Mystic lives as a 1/1. (Without the response
# the same trigger kills it: nowhere-to-run-keeps-its-controllers-own-hexproof-creature-safe-from-the-opponent.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Nowhere to Run
Swamp
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Mother of Runes
Elvish Mystic
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Elvish Mystic)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Elvish Mystic)
Bot2.Colors(Black)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Toughness = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Nowhere to Run.Types = Enchantment
